/-! ## Finite trilinear open-neighbourhood restricted interpolation

The source's four-vertex theorem is a multilinear restricted-type result.
Its summability mechanism is not a per-atom decay at one fixed vertex: each
input amplitude level carries its normalized `L^p` mass.  A genuine open
neighbourhood of restricted input exponents chooses a strict side of the
target exponent independently for the positive and negative dyadic levels.

The following theorem is the three-input analogue of the proved bilinear
open-neighbourhood terminal in the pinned `AHRSUpperBounds` development.  It
is finite, uses no positivity of the trilinear form, and exposes exactly the
endpoint atomwise restricted estimate subsequently needed from the analytic
operator.
-/

